4\. Dat.: the adverbial use of the dat. is rare: aparāya for the future (from ápara later), varāya according to wish (vara choice).

5\. Abl.: these adverbs are seldom formed from substantives, as arat from a distance, asat from near; or from pronouns, amat from near, at then, tat thus, yat as far as; but they are fairly often formed from adjectives, as uttarat from the north, durat from afar, pascat from behind, sanat from of old, saksat visibly.

6\. Gen.: such adverbs are very rare: aktós by night, vástos in the morning.

7\. Loc.: ágre in front, astam-íke at home, áké near, áré afar, rté without, duré afar; aparísu in future.


