a. The first person expresses an intention the execution of which lies in the power of the speaker; e. g. índrasya nú vīryāṇi prá vocam now I will proclaim the heroic deeds of Indra (i. 32¹). Sometimes, however, the execution depends on another; e. g. agníṃ hinvantu no dhíyas: téna jẹṣma dhánaṃ-dhanam let our prayers urge Agni: through him we shall assuredly win booty after booty (x. 156¹).

