In negative sentences the inj. is the only mood (with the exception of the single opt. form bhujema) with which the prohibitive particle mā can be used; e. g. mā na indra párā vṛṇak do not, O Indra, abandon us (viii. 97⁷); viśváyan mā na ā gan let not any swelling thing come near us (vii. 50¹); mā tántuś chedi let not the thread be cut (ii. 28⁵). The aor. form is commoner than the impf. form in the RV., but its relative predominance has greatly increased in the AV.

