In B., however, it is found with the subj. in the sense of a future perfect; e. g. yátra hótā chándasaḥ pāráṃ gáchāt, tát pratiprasthātā prātaranuvākám upā kurutāt when the Hotṛ shall have got to the end of the metre, then let the Pratiprasthātṛ start a Prātaranuvāka (ŚB.).

