B. Secondary Suffixes:

a. Stems in in always accent the suffix; e.g. aśv-in possessing horses.

b. Stems in tama, if superlatives, hardly ever accent the suffix (except puru-tama very many, ut-tama highest, saśvat-tama most frequent), but if ordinals, the final syllable of the suffix; e.g. šata-tama hundredth.

c. Stems in ma, whether superlatives or ordinals, regularly accent the suffix; e.g. adha-ma lowest; asta-ma eighth: except anta-ma next (but twice anta-ma).


