β. A certain number of Tatpuruṣas of syntactical origin, having a genitive case-ending in the first member nearly always followed by páti, are doubly accented; e. g. bṛhas-páti lord of prayer. Other are apāṃ-nápāt son of waters, nárā-śaṃsa (for nárāṃ-śaṃsa) praise of men, śúnaḥ-śépa Dog's tail, name of a man. The analogy of these is followed by some Tatpuruṣas without case-ending in the first member: śácī-páti lord of might; tánū-nápāt son of himself (tanū); nṛ-śaṃsa praise of men.

