*14. Infinitives* are as a rule accented like ordinary cases that would be formed from the same stem.

a. Dative infinitives from stems in i, ti, as, van accent the suffix; those in dhyai, the preceding thematic a; and those formed from the root, the ending; e. g. drśáy-e to see, pītáy-e to drink, carás-e¹ to move, dā-ván-e² to give, tur-ván-e³ to overcome; iy-á-dhyai⁴ to go; drś-é to see.

a. When radical infinitives are compounded with prepositions the root is accented; e. g. sam-idh-e to kindle, abhi-pra-cákṣ-e⁵ to see.

b. The dative infinitive from stems in man, the accusative and the abl. gen. from roots, and all from stems in tu accent the root; e. g. dā-man-e to give;⁶ śúbh-am to shine, ā-sád-am to sit down; ava-pád-as to fall down; dā-tum to give, gán-tos to go, bhár-tav-e to bear, gán-tav-ái⁷ to go.

